      {
        "id": "helpless-duck-76",
        "type": "customfunction",
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5861,
        "width": 160,
        "height": 112,
        "socketArray": [
          {
            "socketType": "in",
            "name": "Code",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"CodeType\"}",
            "data": "(r) => {\n\tconst { brand, noun } = r;\n\treturn `## Brand Name Evaluation\n\nYou are an expert brand strategist with experience in naming tech products and services. I need your professional analysis on a proposed brand name and its associated branded noun.\n\n**Brand Name:** ${brand}\n**Branded Noun:** ${noun}\n*(Example: Twitter is the brand name, Tweet is the branded noun)*\n\nPlease provide a comprehensive evaluation covering:\n\n### Part 1: Brand Name Analysis\n- **Memorability:** How easily remembered is the brand name?\n- **Distinctiveness:** How it stands out from competitors\n- **Pronunciation:** Clarity and ease of saying it aloud\n- **Domain availability:** Likelihood of securing related domains\n- **Semantic meaning:** What it naturally evokes or suggests\n- **International considerations:** Any potential issues in other languages/cultures\n- **Legal concerns:** Potential trademark issues or similarities to existing brands\n\n### Part 2: Branded Noun Analysis\n- **Natural usage:** How naturally it can be used in sentences (\"I just sent a Tweet\")\n- **Verb potential:** Can it function as a verb? (\"I Tweeted about it\")\n- **Clarity:** How clearly it communicates what the user is creating/sharing\n- **Consistency:** How well it aligns with the brand name\n- **Uniqueness:** How distinct it is from common terms\n\n### Part 3: Overall Brand Language\n- **Pros:** Top 3 strengths of this brand name + branded noun combination\n- **Cons:** Top 3 weaknesses or concerns with this combination\n- **Overall rating:** On a scale of 1-10, how effective is this naming strategy?\n\n### Part 4: Alternatives\nSuggest 2-3 alternative combinations of brand name and branded noun that might be more effective, with a brief explanation of why each might work better.\n\nPlease format your response with clear headings and bullet points for easy readability.\n`;\n}",
            "visible": false
          },
          {
            "socketType": "in",
            "name": "Main Thread",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"BooleanType\"}",
            "data": false,
            "visible": false
          },
          {
            "socketType": "in",
            "name": "r",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"StringType\"}"
          },
          {
            "socketType": "out",
            "name": "OutData",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"StringType\"}"
          },
          {
            "socketType": "out",
            "name": "Code",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"CodeType\"}",
            "visible": false
          }
        ],
        "updateBehaviour": {
          "load": true,
          "update": true,
          "interval": false
        },
        "version": 3,
        "name": "Evaluation prompt"
      },
      {
        "id": "answer-markup",
        "name": "Answer",
        "type": "customfunction",
        "x": 640,
        "y": 5861,
        "width": 160,
        "height": 136,
        "socketArray": [
          {
            "socketType": "in",
            "name": "Code",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"CodeType\"}",
            "data": "(content, response, values) => {\n  // values is wired in so this runs on load too: the AI node itself only runs when asked.\n  const escape = (s) => String(s).replace(/[\\\\`*_{}\\[\\]<>#|]/g, '\\\\$&');\n  if (content?.error) {\n    // Turn the errors a first-time visitor will hit into the step that fixes them.\n    const message = String(content.message ?? '');\n    const key = (message.match(/[A-Z]+_API_KEY/) ?? [])[0];\n    if (key) return `**The Companion has no ${key} yet.**\\nOpen the Companion's **Settings**, add your key as ${key} and ask again, or pick a provider you have a key for.`;\n    if (/logged in/i.test(message)) return \"**AI isn't connected yet.**\\nSign in, or use your own key through the Companion.\";\n    if (/fetch|network|load failed|refused/i.test(message)) return \"**Couldn't reach the Tailrmade Companion on this computer.**\\nStart the Companion, or sign in to Tailrmade.\";\n    if (/token|limit|quota/i.test(message)) return \"**Today's AI allowance is used up.**\\nTry again tomorrow, or use your own key through the Companion.\";\n    return `**The AI request failed.**\\n${escape(message)}`;\n  }\n  const text = String(response ?? '').trim();\n  if (!text) return `Press **Ask Claude** for a brand strategist's take on *${escape(values?.brand || 'your brand')}*. An answer takes a few seconds.`;\n  return text;\n}",
            "visible": false
          },
          {
            "socketType": "in",
            "name": "Main Thread",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"BooleanType\"}",
            "data": false,
            "visible": false
          },
          {
            "socketType": "in",
            "name": "content",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"JSONType\"}"
          },
          {
            "socketType": "in",
            "name": "response",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"StringType\"}"
          },
          {
            "socketType": "in",
            "name": "values",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"JSONType\"}"
          },
          {
            "socketType": "out",
            "name": "OutData",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"StringType\"}"
          },
          {
            "socketType": "out",
            "name": "Code",
            "dataType": "{\"class\":\"CodeType\"}",
            "visible": false
          }
        ],
        "updateBehaviour": {
          "load": true,
          "update": true,
          "interval": false
        },
        "version": 3,
        "comment": "Reads Claude's reply, and turns the AI node's errors into the step that fixes them, because a first visit usually has no AI connected yet."
      },
